      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Historically, these ideas were rooted in deeply ingrained, pseudoscientific racial hierarchies used to justify social stratification. Early medical literature often reflected the prevailing racist ideologies of the time, pathologizing entire groups rather than treating individuals. These outdated concepts persist in some academic settings as artifacts of flawed historical thinking, which is why recognizing them as biases is crucial for modern practice.",
      "source": "target",
